{"id": 32, "ts": 1784157851.524796, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fA as the best overall fit. His 100\u202f% reliability, ability to make quick correct decisions, and proven calmness in crisis directly address the core safety and operational reliability criteria. Moreover, he consistently creates a positive crew atmosphere, which supports crew cooperation and professional communication.\nHowever, the discussion has highlighted that Candidate\u202fC brings strong leadership, excellent spatial vision, and the ability to anticipate dangerous situations\u2014attributes that are highly valuable for long\u2011distance operations. The lack of evidence on his openness to feedback, combined with his tendency to be unorganized and sometimes resistant to criticism, raises concerns about adaptability, crew cooperation, and feedback orientation. Without clear proof that he can effectively incorporate crew input and maintain organized procedures, his strengths do not outweigh the comprehensive, proven reliability and decision quality demonstrated by Candidate\u202fA.\nTherefore, unless further evidence emerges showing that Candidate\u202fC can reliably manage feedback and maintain organization under long\u2011haul conditions, I continue to support Candidate\u202fA."}
